          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "A 128-bit AES key detected. Grover's algorithm gives a quadratic speed-up to brute-force key search, so AES-128 drops to roughly 64 bits of quantum security. NIST still accepts AES-128 today (it is the reference point for post-quantum security category 1), but long-lived secrets and frameworks such as NSA CNSA 2.0 call for AES-256."
          },
